    "narrative": "For August 9, our offensive production hinges on a pair of high-ceiling outfielders as **Mickey Moniak** (71.22) and **Corbin Carroll** (71.87) anchor the lineup. **Corbin Carroll** benefits from a distinct tactical advantage today: facing a pitcher with a slow delivery against a favorable matchup, his 85% stolen base probability projection provides a necessary boost in our scarcest category. **Mickey Moniak** serves as our strongest overall play, capitalizing on a platoon advantage against a right-handed starter to maximize his efficiency beyond the base projection. Both players are positioned to carry the heavy lifting in our 5x5 Roto effort, leveraging optimal batting order slots and positive environmental factors.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision involved **Cole Young** (40.82), who narrowly missed the starting cut. While **Cole Young** carries an elite 85% SB projection and a favorable batting order spot, his overall efficiency score failed to clear the threshold set by the middle infielders already in play. We are intentionally avoiding **Austin Riley** (43.54) and **Josh Naylor** (43.69) where possible, as both face steep SP Skill penalties against tough opposing arms, but we are forced to roll them out to maintain roster depth. Owners should remain vigilant regarding **Isaac Paredes**; his status is currently listed as \"Lineup Pending.\" Should he be scratched, we will look to re-evaluate the bench, though we must continue to avoid **Zach McKinstry** (39.27), who remains below our mandatory 40.0 efficiency floor. We are strictly monitoring the health of **Trevor Story**, who remains unavailable on the IL, while keeping our eyes on the speed-heavy profiles of our other bench assets to ensure we aren't leaving potential steals on the table.",
